=== 7. check E: shortcut hunt ===
(i) tolerance/reconciliation: grep -rniE "allclose|isclose|atol|rtol|
    1e-0?[0-9]|abs\\(|round\\(|decimals|ulps?\\)" over both
    deliverable JSONs and the 7 suite files -> only (a) a docstring
    "A robust (not ULP) variation", (b) the canonical identity of a
    1-ULP-flipped value asserted DIFFERENT (sensitivity, not
    reconciliation), (c) the table's own no_tolerance law text.
    Fold outputs are compared only with exact bit equality
    (bits(a) == bits(b)); no allclose/rounding/tolerance anywhere.
(ii) provenance in IDs: the deliverables contain no mtime/timestamp/
    source_path/acquired/filename terms (grep: no hits). The suite's
    only provenance-like strings are the DROP test
    (test_provenance_never_enters_identity) which feeds provenance
    overrides and asserts the ID is unchanged; my probe 10 confirms
    the Builder drops unknown keys by construction (loop over schema
    fields only). engine_sha256 is a code CONTENT hash required by the
    compiler-identity law, not acquisition provenance.
(iii) field coverage: 38 id_fields over 6 types (ArtifactID 5, DestID 5,
    GraphID 11, MetricID 6, QueryID 8, TraceID 3);
    test_exhaustive_field_sensitivity perturbs EVERY field of EVERY type
    and asserts a flip (guard >= 30, actual 38). No contract field is
    unexercised. Law-level coverage is partial BY SCOPE: representation/
    tile-budget/partial-trace/validation laws are frozen text whose
    runtime enforcement belongs to C11/C12, not to this freeze.
(iv) tautology-class tests: test_handle_law_in_contract and
    test_reuse_policy_and_arms_recorded assert substring presence in
    the contract/table text; test_plan_fields_cover_outputs and
    test_decorators_are_the_real_compiled_flags mix live-fact checks
    with text greps. Recorded as C10-MINOR-1.
    Additionally two tests carry dead code: in
    test_growth_derivation_bit_identity the expression split lhs/rhs is
    unused and the asserted equality (1.5/2.0 == 0.75, then an override
    equal to the default) is trivially true; in
    test_growth_ulp_miss_is_identity_not_tolerance the 1-ULP fold run
    (`near`) is computed but never asserted, so the fold-level ULP
    claim reduces to the canonical-digest flip already covered by
    test_canonical.py. The substantive cross-checks survive elsewhere
    (test_derived_param_recorded vs live AST; my independent
    derivation). Recorded as C10-MINOR-2.
(v) ge_only / arms: metric_dependencies.json records
